CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static_assert condition could not be evaluated
--
An UNNAMED function parameter pack (`Args...`) was not expanded when the
function template was instantiated (the expansion keyed on the declarator's
name), so the instance had one parameter; a two-argument call never matched
its type and constexpr evaluation of `count(1, 'c')` failed ("static_assert
condition could not be evaluated").  Also covers a constexpr member template
on a constexpr object and a constrained variadic overload.  Non-vacuous: the
last assertion states a wrong value and must FAIL.
